NNAAMMEE
       nsec3hash - generate NSEC3 hash

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       nnsseecc33hhaasshh {salt} {algorithm} {iterations} {domain}

       nnsseecc33hhaasshh --rr {algorithm} {flags} {iterations} {salt} {domain}

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       nnsseecc33hhaasshh  generates  an NSEC3 hash based on a set of NSEC3 parameters.
       This can be used to check the validity of NSEC3  records  in  a  signed
       zone.

       If  this  command is invoked as nnsseecc33hhaasshh --rr, it takes arguments in or‐
       der, matching the first four fields of an NSEC3 record followed by  the
       domain  name: aallggoorriitthhmm, ffllaaggss, iitteerraattiioonnss, ssaalltt, ddoommaaiinn. This makes it
       convenient to copy and paste a portion of an NSEC3 or NSEC3PARAM record
       into a command line to confirm the correctness of an NSEC3 hash.

AARRGGUUMMEENNTTSS
       ssaalltt   This is the salt provided to the hash algorithm.

       aallggoorriitthhmm
              This is a number indicating the hash  algorithm.  Currently  the
              only supported hash algorithm for NSEC3 is SHA-1, which is indi‐
              cated by the number 1; consequently "1" is the only useful value
              for this argument.

       ffllaaggss  This  is  provided for compatibility with NSEC3 record presenta‐
              tion format, but is ignored since the flags do  not  affect  the
              hash.

       iitteerraattiioonnss
              This  is  the number of additional times the hash should be per‐
              formed.

       ddoommaaiinn This is the domain name to be hashed.

